              "message": "Shortcuts: use the shared craft-keymap crate for the catalogue, overrides, dispatch and .kys import (#3119)\n\n* Shortcuts: the keymap, overrides and dispatch come from craft-keymap\n\nThe editor's catalogue (commands, UI commands, panels, tools; one tool\ngroup per tool; show/hide commands marked as toggles) builds a\ncraft-keymap Keymap. UiState::shortcut_overrides is a craft_keymap\nOverrides stored through keymap::stored, which writes the same map of\nentry key -> one string as before, with panel: keys and VectorCraft's\nspellings, so earlier versions read the file; a value that is not text\ndrops that entry instead of every preference.\n\nKey presses run through craft_keymap's Dispatcher with accept filters:\nkeys that type text go to the one-key text path, and while the Type\ntool edits only command-key chords run. Held keys repeat. Conflicts\nand assignment use the crate's conflicts and set_bindings. Extra Shift\nno longer falls back to the chord without it.\n\n* Shortcuts: .kys import matches and applies through craft-keymap\n\nThe review proposes targets with craft_keymap's namematch, and Apply\nhands the ready rows to craft_keymap::plan as one set, each row's\ntarget passed as the remembered answer for its entry. The later row\ntakes a chord, and commands outside the set lose the chords the set\ngives. Rows with one name in one block keep their own targets.\nThe engine's own namematch module is removed.\n\n* Shortcuts: Cmd+, beside other hits, web Mac platform, cached dialog view\n\n- Pin craft-keymap at 362eb59f.\n- Cmd+, opens Settings on a Mac after the frame's other shortcuts run, with the\n  Mac read from egui's OS; drop settings_chord, which dispatch no longer used.\n- The web build follows the browser's OS, so Ctrl stays Ctrl on a Mac.\n- The Keyboard Shortcuts dialog keeps its keymap, row texts and conflict count\n  between frames while the working set is unchanged.\n- Every default shortcut text becomes its entry's binding (test).\n- craft-keymap counts as a UI crate for the layer check.\n- Translate \"too many changed shortcuts\"; the parse error reuses the existing\n  \"can't parse shortcut `{c}`\" message.\n\n* Shortcuts: the chords the operating system takes can't be assigned\n\nThe keymap reserves craft_keymap::reserved::system for its platform:\nwindow switching and closing, and the virtual consoles off the Mac.\nThe Keyboard Shortcuts dialog and shortcuts.set refuse them with\n\"<chord> is reserved by the system\", and a saved override on one keeps\nthe entry's default. No default shortcut uses a reserved chord.\n\n* Shortcuts: craft-keymap at craft-libs 2eca9b3a\n\ncraft-keymap comes from storytold/craft-libs (craft-libs #164 and #186), at the rev craft-pdf\nalready uses. The web build keeps the browser's full platform, so Windows browsers get Windows'\nreserved chords, and each platform caches its own default keymap.",
              "url": "https://github.com/Blenux/vectorcraft/commit/8bf090b25389b48aa6f9d7415de57c9ce7ccf8cb",
              "date": "2026-10-24T19:01:26Z"
